# v21 OVERLAY = v20 (declared arrival, junction goals 0.85, v18's lane terms,
# live encoder, idle 2.0) with ONE change: a wrong declaration is a FINE, not
# the end of the episode. Sourced after v52_reward.env.
. "$REPO/slurm/v20_overlay.env"

# 9. FALSE_STOP_PENALTY=5 (user 2026-10-28, "rerun" after v20 failed).
#
#    v20 scored 0.000 on 120 Town02 eval episodes (100k, 200k, 300k) while
#    driving a median 13.9 m towards goals 21.8 m away. Ending the episode on a
#    wrong declaration forfeits every reward the car would still have earned,
#    so "never declare" was the safe policy: in training only 47 arrivals in
#    893 goal episodes and none in the last 100, and the eval -- which drives
#    the mean action -- never declared at all, making the score exactly zero
#    however well it drove. Habitat can afford that rule at 200M steps; we have
#    10M.
#
#    At 5 the fine is a quarter of a lane crossing (20) and a tenth of the
#    arrival bonus (50): declaring is cheap enough to try, expensive enough not
#    to spam. Declaring AT the goal is unchanged: +50 and the episode ends.
export FALSE_STOP_PENALTY=5.0
